{"name":"Cattle Drive","hex":"#bb7b51","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cattle drive","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process of transporting a herd of bovine animals (such as bulls, cows, or steers) by compelling them to walk across a significant distance of countryside, under the escort of drovers on horseback and often over a period of days.","A trail or route used for the movement of herds of cattle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cattle_drive"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cattle Drive","blocks":[{"text":"Cattle Drive is a 1951 American Western film directed by Kurt Neumann and starring Joel McCrea, Dean Stockwell and Chill Wills. Much of the film was shot in Death Valley National Park, California and Paria, Utah."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/Cattle_Drive_FilmPoster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cattle_Drive"},{"title":"Droving","blocks":[{"text":"Droving is the practice of walking livestock over long distances. It is a type of herding, often associated with cattle, in which case it is a cattle drive. Droving stock to market—usually on foot and often with the aid of dogs—has a very long history. An owner might entrust an agent to deliver stock to market and bring back the proceeds. There has been droving since people in cities found it necessary to source food from distant supplies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Morning_by_ST_Gill.jpg/330px-Morning_by_ST_Gill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Droving"},{"title":"Cattle","blocks":[{"text":"Cattle are large, domesticated, bovid ungulates widely kept as livestock. They are prominent modern members of the subfamily Bovinae and the most widespread species of the genus Bos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Cow_%28Fleckvieh_breed%29_Oeschinensee_Slaunger_2009-07-07.jpg/330px-Cow_%28Fleckvieh_breed%29_Oeschinensee_Slaunger_2009-07-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cattle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Drovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_%2811313111916%29.jpg/500px-Drovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_%2811313111916%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Drovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_%2811313111916%29.jpg/500px-Drovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_%2811313111916%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Drovers in New Zealand c. 1950","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADrovers_rest_their_horses_and_dogs_(11313111916).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cattle_round_up.jpg/500px-Cattle_round_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cattle_round_up.jpg/1280px-Cattle_round_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cattle_round_up.jpg/500px-Cattle_round_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A modern small-scale cattle drive in New Mexico, U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACattle_round_up.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Edwin_Henry_Landseer_%281802-1873%29_-_The_Drover%27s_Departure%2C_A_Scene_in_the_Grampians_-_FA.88%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg/500px-Edwin_Henry_Landseer_%281802-1873%29_-_The_Drover%27s_Departure%2C_A_Scene_in_the_Grampians_-_FA.88%28O%29_-_Victoria_and_Albert_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser